						<td class="headline" align="left"><a name="#777">Guildrules</a></td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td class="body">
							We are Ancient Honor. We are a guild of Honor. Honor is not well-taught in this society, but we know what's right. Do what you know is right and you can't go wrong. I say  Ancient Honor is a guild loosely built on the idealic rules of chivalry. <br />
<br />
I'm Olivera, guildleader of Ancient Honor. My goal for this guild is to become a guild standard, what every other guild strives to be and what people expect in a guild.  I don't want to be the biggest guild on the E'ci server, I want to be the best.  <br />
<br />
Why are we together? We each bring unique gifts to the guild. We bring our experiences, our insight and our viewpoints. We help each other, and all we meet, as we travel around the spheres.  <br />
<br />
General behavior<br />
<br />
You are the single-most important advertising tool the guild has. You are the face of the Ancient Honor;  you are our representative in the field. As long as you are out there, we expect you to be a credit to us. All of the normal rules of the game apply. No Kill-Stealing, etc. We hold every member to the standard of adult behavior--the minimum playing age is supposed to be 13, but we will treat you as an adult and expect you to behave as such. If an officer gets a tell about your behavior, we will speak to you privately about it. This  shouldn't have to occur more than once. Any officer may, at his/her  discretion, remove anyone from the guild if necessary or summon other officers to Ancienthonorcourt for disciplinary action. If you think you've been unfarily removed, you can appeal the decision to me, but that decision will be final. We shouldn't have to remove anyone, and we'd regret having to do so.<br />
<br />
Watch your language<br />
<br />
I'm no prude, but remember that there are some younger people playing the game. I wouldn't want to see someone banned from the game because their mom saw a naughty word or three on the screen. General rule: If someone would probably object to the words, don't say them. There are several hundred thousand words in the English language...use some of them, instead.<br />
<br />
Help everyone and anyone, regardless of their guild<br />
<br />
We all travel thru the lands and see many characters. Do what you can to help them. Carry extra food and drink, or summon it, for those who run out...refuse the payment, do it because you care. We have limited playing time, so the time you give to another is all the more precious. Those few minutes you spend helping someone, just for the heck of it, will be impressive upon possible recruits.<br />
<br />
<br />
Begging from the guild <br />
<br />
While there is a begging skill built into the game, the experience comes from begging NPCs. Begging is beneath you. You have every opportunity to make of yourself what you will; you have the power to attain anything in the game--when you are ready to get it. You do not need the latest uberweapon and armor to play...Use what you have, you'll get there. If you are not of a level to, at least, attempt the item by yourself, don't ask the guild to get it for you. We are here to support you: we'll help you get your corpse back, we'll get you a rez, we will help you start out again if you lose everything. But committing the guild to get your desired weapon before you're able to use it is not going to happen. Sorry.<br />
<br />
Auctioning in Guildsay<br />
<br />
Let's just not do that. Open a guildauction channel and those interested can join it. <br />
<br />
<br />
Guild entry requirements<br />
<br />
New members must be at least level 30 or greater, any exception subject to my approval.  Current member alternate characters may be invited at any level. <br />
<br />
Officer Requirements<br />
Any new officer candidates must be level 45 or greater and have been in the guild at least 90 days.  <br />
<br />
If you have any questions, comments, suggestions, complaints, feel free to contact me directly in the game or email me at Oliveraaloevera@aol.com.<br />
<br />
<br />
Once you've read these rules, please go to the Guildrules thread on the message board and acknowledge you read and understand this.<br />
<br />
Thanks!<br />
Ollie
